## Kithix

Scope: completed 12.1 Week9 Story (220), LFR (17), Normal (14), and Heroic routing. Mythic is not validated by these plans. Current module inspected on 2026-10-20; no new OCR/replay performed during consolidation.

### Shared lifecycle and warning ownership

- Keep `timersEasy` for Story/LFR/Normal with explicit difficulty differences, and separate Heroic rules. Later completion notes supersede old Heroic-only and no-Normal plan restrictions. Preserve the user's `statTypes = "story,normal,heroic,mythic"` independently of routing coverage.
- Use raw duration for `TLStart` and scheduled completion; rounded buckets are routing keys, not permission to discard decimals. Runtime IDs own lifecycles, not ability identity.
- Premature state-2 Horrors/Grasp/Null Gate events use per-ID scheduled completion with bugged-event marking. Ignore their premature finish; finish counts at the raw deadline. Preserve bar/count ownership, unscheduling, bugged-ID removal, and retained core mapping cleanup on finish/cancel.
- A tracked phase-1 cancellation batch clears all stage-1 schedules, including prematurely terminal rows that receive no subsequent cancel. Guard stage-2 transition against repeats; clear add window, old schedules, bars, and reservations before entering it. Also clean on fallback/combat end.
- Preserve the cross-pull `badStateDetected` failure latch: engage/end reset routing counters and schedules, not this latch. Unknown routes use full fallback with debug notification, not passthrough. Hidden bars retain timeline-only metadata during valid hardcoded engage; unsupported difficulties retain normal fallback.
- Divine Radiance is 1303169; Abyssal Grasp is 1303406 with its own timer. Preserve personal aura audio for Horrors, Grasp, Null Gate, and Negation rather than adding duplicate completion announcements.
- Dark Devastation's hardcoded tank warning checks verified boss1 precisely. Voidswarm completion arms generic add warnings; Darkness completion disarms them. Preserve the option/window guards and boss2-4 cast/channel registrations; slots can become eggs, so never infer ability identity from the unit token.
- Reuse `AddSecretGenericWarning`. Current Kithix passes target-only sound policy through `UnitIsUnit("target", unit)`; do not replace it with the older helper proposal's default-sound call.

### Story/LFR/Normal routing

- Stage 1 shared buckets: Voidswarm 5; Appendage 15/21/34; Devastation 20/22/77; Extinguish 31/62. Normal additionally has Devastation 23/54.
- Story/LFR raw 45 first means Devastation, then Radiance. Normal 45 means Radiance only. Raw 57 first means Darkness, then Extinguish. Rounded 119 alternates Voidswarm then Darkness in ADDED order; raw 119 is truly shared, and Story Voidswarm also has 118.999. Preserve/reset all three ambiguity counters.
- LFR/Normal additionally use opening Horrors 40 and Grasp 67; scheduled premature-finish recurrences are Horrors 37/82 and Grasp 30/89. Story must not gain these routes merely because it shares the router.
- Story enters stage 2 on 121-second Eclipse, without inventing a Null Gate from absent evidence. LFR/Normal enter on the first 3-second Null Gate; 61 is Eclipse thereafter.
- LFR stage-2 10 always means scheduled Null Gate, including the first occurrence; no Negation was observed in that corpus. Normal stage-2 first 10 means Negation, later 10 scheduled Null Gate; 15 also means Negation. Do not apply Normal/Heroic's first-10 rule to LFR.

### Heroic routing

- Stage 1: Voidswarm 5; Appendage 12/15/18/32; Devastation 20/22/69; Extinguish 57; opening Horrors 37 with scheduled 33/76 recurrences; opening Grasp 62 with scheduled 27/82 recurrences; Radiance 40.
- True raw collisions require ADDED-order counters: 29 opens with Extinguish then Appendage; 52 opens with Darkness then Extinguish; rounded 109 alternates Voidswarm then Darkness. Raw 109 is shared; Darkness also has 108.999.
- First 3-second Null Gate enters stage 2. Stage-2 15 is Negation; identical raw 10 opens with Negation then scheduled Null Gate recasts; 61 is Eclipse.

### Regression anchors and evidence limits

- Recorded corpus: Heroic Kill/Wipe1/Wipe2 (67/31/50 additions), Story kill (23), LFR kill (32), Normal kill (38). Prior replay coverage includes visible/hidden bars, consecutive pulls, real module/core helper loading, and synthetic lifecycle/fallback/window tests. These are saved results, not tests rerun here.
- Preserve Heroic event 332 at 37.01 with raw 32.999 Horrors and immediate state 2; it must not finish early. Keep exact raw collision classes, stage-2 10 ordering, no double finishes, no stale stage-1 callbacks, and unsupported-difficulty/failure-latch tests.
- Story phase-1 cancel batch is 166.42, with Eclipse 121 added at 174.43. LFR cancel batch 159.37 must also clear already-terminal scheduled Grasp 49 and Horrors 54; first stage-2 Null Gate/Eclipse arrive at 167.38. LFR scheduled 10s Null Gates at 170.39/180.40 must not finish immediately; kill 188.76 cancels the last before its deadline.
- Normal transition 165.62 cancels schedules 24/30; Null Gate 35 completes 186.65, 37 completes 196.66, and 38 is killed before 206.64. Preserve raw Extinguish 56.999 and recorded kill boundary 197.49.
- Saved plans record repaired canonical OCR caches and image-confirmed premature finishes/centisecond jitter. Those anomalies are not unresolved OCR by themselves; follow the OCR procedure before new log interpretation. Generic warning secret sinks still require live-client verification.

